  message: "DONE in PR #2044 (dev 2dbb650f14); record docs/measurements/0032-analysed-repository-as-taint-source.md; lab /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/pakag_11042026. (1) HOW REPO CONTENT ENTERS: fs_read mints no label by design, so docs/hypergumbo-self-catalog/repo_content_sources.yaml declares analysed_repo_content as a caller-seeded source on discovery (find_files, find_non_test_files, FileIndex views); the pathlib.read_text anchor was tried and REJECTED by measurement (it labels the tracker package's own reads: 7 network, 161 subprocess flows, none the analysed repository). (2) THE CLAIMS: five repo-content-no-{host-fs,network,subprocess,install-artifact,dev-zone} shipped, all confirmed_with_caveats on dev, sanitized flows exactly the entry claims' (5 host_fs, 100 subprocess): every seed sits inside a runtime cmd_* closure, so they add no reachability fact and NAME the threat with the same caveats; snapshot re-recorded (23), SECURITY.md regenerated. FINDING ON THE WAY: the zone barrier is declared per label with no wildcard, so the first run read VIOLATED on 105 wrapper internals (a violated-for-the-wrong-reason); transform added, test_self_catalog_barrier_coverage.py pins the pairing (red against the pre-edit file). (3) MEASURED LIMIT, as pre-registered: the matcher carries no argument identity; a name-in-path fixture and a content-in-content fixture produce byte-identical evidence, so the POSITION half of the sentence is not expressible. Reading every permitted-zone flow at its sink finds three sites where a repo-chosen value is a path/argv component (git ls-tree HEAD -- <dir>; the sanitized route path in a handler-slice filename; hashed git metadata in cache dir names), each contained by a code fact, none by a claim. Design decision filed as WI-tahuv-lapal-likur-ginab-nabis-gakal-mibir-kukil. NOT ASSERTED: anything about rows the untyped-receiver caveat hides (74.1% of method sites), or the position half."  # 8652
